title ALES153 — Lotus's stereo_smooth_runs: the run-length smoother carried into stereo, two independent hysteresis holds, the analysis-corner lift bound to ALES101 by the stereo smooth law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Third rung this turn (after ALES152 stereo_collapse_silence, sent). The ascending Lotus crux is ALES101 (smooth_runs — the smoothing hysteresis ALES95 named as a later rung, absorb every run shorter than a minimum into what surrounds it) carried into stereo. Crux-first and Lindy-first agree: smoothing is the robustness move that turns a per-frame reader into a usable segmenter, the natural companion to ALES147's stereo segmenter before any stereo VAD reads it.
think Unlike ALES148-152, this meets NO desync wall — smooth_runs is READ-ONLY over the labels, rewriting a run-length sequence and touching no PCM, changing no clip length. So its honest stereo shape is the analysis-corner one ALES146 (stereo_voiced) and ALES147 (stereo_segment) took: run the proven mono smoother on each channel independently, keeping the two results apart in a StereoSegments{left,right}. The two channels flicker independently (ALES147 proved their segmentations differ in count and boundary), so they smooth independently — a tick on the left is absorbed by the left's neighbours, never the right's.
think Implementation composes ALES101's mono smooth_runs twice, once per side of the StereoSegments, with one shared min_run; StereoSmoothError = ALES101's SmoothError reused whole (the honest unreachable SegmentsFull, since smoothing only merges). Seam asserts both input sides within max_segments on entry, both output sides never grow past their input count or the ceiling on exit; the per-run tiling/coalesced contract is asserted inside ALES101 itself. The stereo smooth law is proven against ALES101's mono smooth_runs directly (a second call per channel) across nine min_run values with a flickering left and a clean right; independence, identical-channels, degenerate (min_run 0 identity, empty channel empty, single run unchanged, span-coalesce carrying first verdict), and a grounded-in-the-segmenter case all GREEN; each output channel checked as data by an independent well_smoothed reference.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded run-length label sequences, read-only over labels (no PCM touched), a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red. Recorded lesson: a mono rewrite that is read-only over the labels (not the samples) carries into stereo by the ANALYSIS-corner shape (per-channel independence, each side equal to the mono reader) rather than the EDIT-corner lockstep shape ALES148-152 needed — because no length changes, the balance invariant is never at risk, so the two channels simply stay apart. This distinguishes the two families of stereo lift cleanly: length-changing edits lockstep on the joint silence, label-only rewrites run per channel. Witness GREEN (stereo smooth law across nine min_runs, independence, identical channels, degenerate, span-coalesce, grounded), TAME style bans clean. Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES153 roster token appended to the Status line).
